WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.738
Hi! 12 biscuits shared equally among 3 children. How many each? Today we'll learn division.

2
00:00:09.888 --> 00:00:13.434
Sharing equally means every share is the same.

3
00:00:13.584 --> 00:00:17.946
Give one biscuit to each child in turn until none are left.

4
00:00:18.096 --> 00:00:20.418
Each child gets 4.

5
00:00:20.568 --> 00:00:25.698
As division: 12 divided by 3 is 4.

6
00:00:25.848 --> 00:00:30.546
12 biscuits, 3 in each bag. How many bags?

7
00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:36.786
Count in threes: 3, 6, 9, 12. That's 4 bags.

8
00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:40.626
This is also 12 divided by 3 is 4.

9
00:00:40.776 --> 00:00:46.578
Check with times: 4 times 3 is 12. Correct.

10
00:00:46.728 --> 00:00:51.114
Watch out! Equal sharing means every share matches!

11
00:00:51.264 --> 00:00:55.626
5, 4 and 3 aren't equal, so it isn't equal sharing.

12
00:00:55.776 --> 00:00:59.466
4 each is equal sharing.

13
00:00:59.616 --> 00:01:09.906
Your turn! 10 apples shared equally by 2 people. How many each? Pause and think.

14
00:01:10.056 --> 00:01:16.338
10 divided by 2 is 5: 5 each. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:16.488 --> 00:01:25.098
Another one! What is 15 divided by 5? Pause and think.

16
00:01:25.248 --> 00:01:31.146
3 fives are 15, so it's 3. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:31.296 --> 00:01:39.546
Here's another! What is 8 divided by 4? Pause and think.

18
00:01:39.696 --> 00:01:45.210
2 fours are 8, so it's 2. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:55.794
Try one more! 20 pens, 5 in each box. How many boxes? Pause and think.

20
00:01:55.944 --> 00:02:03.066
5, 10, 15, 20: 4 boxes. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:03.216 --> 00:02:11.802
Try one more! What is 18 divided by 2? Pause and think.

22
00:02:11.952 --> 00:02:17.922
9 twos are 18, so it's 9. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:18.072 --> 00:02:26.922
Try one more! Is 6, 6, 6 an equal share? Pause and think.

24
00:02:27.072 --> 00:02:32.538
Each share is 6, so yes. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:32.688 --> 00:02:43.554
Last one! 16 biscuits shared equally by 4 people. How many each? Pause and think.

26
00:02:43.704 --> 00:02:50.274
16 divided by 4 is 4: 4 each. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:50.424 --> 00:02:56.538
Remember: division is sharing equally. Check your answer with multiplication.

28
00:02:56.688 --> 00:03:01.362
Next time you share snacks, share them equally!

